msgid "Tarot Gimbal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:7
#: 5736549e09cb41b686ea685215a110d1
msgid "**ARCHIVED** .. note::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:18
#: 4b2b54389a7141b8862754f091cac799
msgid "The instructions below recommend using `Tarot Gimbal Firmware v1.5 <https://download.ardupilot.org/downloads/wiki/advanced_user_tools/ZYX-BMGC-EN_V1.5.zip>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:21
#: e96ca02705a54ad48eda7792aca89fd5
msgid "Connecting to the Autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:26
#: 0e2aa01e86554795adc2f66d61d976ec
msgid "The Tarot gimbal's red and black power wires should be connected directly to a 2S or 3S battery. If you plan to use 4S (or higher), please use a voltage regulator to ensure the voltage stays within safe operating limits: DC 7.4 V - 14.8 V (recommended 12 V). 3DR RTF Quad, Y6, and X8 include a voltage regular to allow use of 4S batteries with the Tarot gimbal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:27
#: 427fb643a53e4f70ba1dd05a59de5bf0
msgid "The \"T\" pin should be connected to the Pixhawk's AUX1 signal pin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:28
#: 02257bceaa2c4967a95e6c97a094130d
msgid "One of the two \"-\" pins should be connected to the Pixhawk's AUX1 ground pin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:31
#: 3ba52bf6e2ca4be6b2021f876b120848
msgid "Operation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:33
#: 3da2dea1d3454d60afa437dc59a4668e
msgid "Paper instructions are normally provided with the gimbal but a slightly out of date user manual can be found in the \"User Manual\" directory of the `Tarot Gimbal Firmware v1.5 zip <https://download.ardupilot.org/downloads/wiki/advanced_user_tools/ZYX-BMGC-EN_V1.5.zip>`__ file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:36
#: cd3c913b25d44839932488fd71fe63c4
msgid "Upon powering your vehicle, the gimbal will display a solid yellow light while it is starting and calibrating. Do not touch the gimbal while it is starting up. When the gimbal displays a blinking blue light, it is ready for flight. If the gimbal is not connected to the autopilot, it will perform basic stabilization without autopilot control, indicated by a solid blue light."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:43
#: 35d77cab2ead4c64a7c3a43fc6ed928a
msgid "**LED meanings**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:45
#: 5c0c4a826a734c27955fcce38ba0fd0a
msgid "Solid yellow      = calibrating"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:46
#: 00595ca4a14a4b619c03279f3749f265
msgid "Blinking blue      = ready, connected to autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:47
#: d5a4fb85449b42a1a29871dfdf0b8bd2
msgid "Solid blue     = ready, not connected to autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:50
#: 7df22ed910b346a881d85f2a02093b1f
msgid "Configuring the Gimbal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:52
#: f2ac04c1f5334ee2b35608e5c0942446
msgid "Tarot gimbals normally work out of the box but if you wish to change the gimbal's internal configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:55
#: 405202f0708e4e0ba44a95f6f0b498aa
msgid "Use the provided USB dongle to connect the Gimbal board to your computer (Windows only).  If this is the first time you have plugged in the dongle you will likely see a USB device installation window. After successful installation of the driver a new COM port named \"Prolific USB-to-Serial Comm Port\" should appear in the Device Manager as shown below.  If drivers cannot be found you may be able to install Windows 7 or Windows XP drivers using one of the .exe files found in the \"driver\" directory of the `Tarot Gimbal Firmware v1.5 zip <https://download.ardupilot.org/downloads/wiki/advanced_user_tools/ZYX-BMGC-EN_V1.5.zip>`__ file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:71
#: 0831a7d1fce84ad49eec64b08bee3c76
msgid "Windows 8 and 10 users may find issues with the Prolific USB-to-Serial driver not starting.  This issue can apparently be resolved according by `following instructions on this web page: <http://leftbraintinkering.blogspot.com/2013/05/usb-to-serial-prolific-2303-device.html>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:73
#: 38cbd93514484adc9a7e5d10031bb437
msgid "Download and unzip the `Tarot Gimbal Firmware v1.5 zip <https://download.ardupilot.org/downloads/wiki/advanced_user_tools/ZYX-BMGC-EN_V1.5.zip>`__ file to a convenient place on your computer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:74
#: 2f619d7e6e6c4d8ebb8f6b3bb8b9e36f
msgid "Double click on the **ZYX-BMGC-EN_V1.5.exe** file (found in the above zip) and the configuration UI shown below should appear"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:79
#: 14c951d5fff14bc38faacc843db50d03
msgid "Power the Gimbal by plugging in the battery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:80
#: c557aa0d6f0d4ccdbfb1fb12623f31e4
msgid "In the configuration UI, select the COM port and press the **Open COM Port** button.  After a few seconds the image of the camera should begin moving as the gimbal is moved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:81
#: 9a6d6ad204964b41895913732cd5a402
msgid "The most important setting is to set the **Default Mode** (just above COM port drop-down) to **Default Mode: stick position mode**.  Select this and press **Write Settings To Flash**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:84
#: 394e865e3d9042e5b01b501571c6863c
msgid "Set-up through the Ground Station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:89
#: f723e027230441c99cb07c5371ee3e58
msgid "If using the Mission Planner a Camera Gimbal setup screen is available as shown above:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:91
#: c2e47075d63e47d09c4565e4a8c35549
msgid "\"Type\" should be set to \"Servo\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:92
#: 274deb2ec2c24bda8dd0821b6524e937
msgid "\"Pitch\" should be set to \"SERVO9\" to specify AUX OUT 1 is connected to the gimbal's pitch input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:93
#: 6d5e1b454f764a2bbb3fd4de70f3d0cd
msgid "\"Stabilize Pitch\" should be unchecked"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:94
#: 8721f15195f94d6dafc0a9fe71e79ef3
msgid "\"Servo Limits\" holds the minimum and maximum PWM values that will be sent to the gimbal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:95
#: b1e16cd7fdf548cbbe6d170a69c0d698
msgid "\"Angle Limits\" are the earth-frame angles (in degrees) that the gimbal can achieve. \"0\" degrees is straight ahead, \"-90\" is straight down"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:97
#: d72a1408dcbf476da3dfb70c2469e588
msgid "If manually setting parameters for the first mount:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:99
#: 34c086351e0e4583ae0cf6fe20a8dc8c
msgid ":ref:`MNT1_TYPE <MNT1_TYPE>` = 1 (for \"Servo\" gimbal)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:100
#: 5e9e60b8f3774d4a9a086bcf7a3ef3fe
msgid ":ref:`RC6_OPTION <RC6_OPTION>` = 213 to specify that RC input channel 6 (normally the tuning knob) will be used to control the pitch of the gimbal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:101
#: beb08a8980954a92b9ef427a2db86af0
msgid ":ref:`MNT1_PITCH_MAX <MNT1_PITCH_MAX>` = 0 to specify the gimbal's highest angle is zero degrees (i.e. forward)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:102
#: 60a7ba87ed6d46d2bb24d8e01b5263c7
msgid ":ref:`MNT1_PITCH_MIN <MNT1_PITCH_MIN>` = -90 to specify the gimbal's lowest angle is 90 degrees (i.e. down)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:103
#: 5e13d50b392e4ed3bcebc50156b6e62a
msgid ":ref:`SERVO9_MIN <SERVO9_MIN>` = 1000 to specify the minimum PWM value to send to the gimbal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:104
#: 492a5bef19954465818eff6057128655
msgid ":ref:`SERVO9_MAX <SERVO9_MAX>` = 1520 to specify the maximum PWM value to send to the gimbal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:109
#: 1637bbb89a4b40128d9aefbdaf6a78dc
msgid "Testing the gimbal moves correctly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:111
#: 9e5014e7f6334fae976d008d3e41a0dd
msgid "**Testing the pilot's control of pitch**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:113
#: 40a1994c5c074645972819703c07d5ee
msgid "Once powered the gimbal should point to its Pitch Angle Min (i.e. straight down) when your transmitter's channel 6 tuning knob is at its minimum pwm value (perhaps around 1000) and the camera should point to its maximum pitch angle (i.e. straight forward) when the tuning knob is at its maximum (perhaps around 2000). The mission planner's Radio calibration page can be used to check the Ch6's current input pwm value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:115
#: 8e4b8cd9d0b04d0088c2fea3883e9cd3
msgid "**Testing ROI**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:117
#: 3ff44e17f9324705b2ac79e8dd645603
msgid "**You must have GPS lock to test ROI.** The ROI feature points the vehicle and/or camera to point at a target. The instructions above describe a setup so that only controls the pitch of the Tarot gimbal so when a :ref:`Do-Set-ROI <copter:mission-command-list_do-set-roi>` command is received Copter will attempt to turn the vehicle's nose to point in the direction of the target and pitch the camera depending upon the vehicle's distance and altitude. You can test the gimbal pitch moves correctly by connecting with the mission planner, then on the Flight Data screen's map, right-mouse-button-click on a point about 50m ahead of the vehicle (the orange and red lines show the vehicle's current heading), select \"Point Camera Here\" and input an altitude of -50 (meters). This should cause the gimbal to point down at about 45 degrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:122
#: 1ed48fa91e17420c863d3ed482632f02
msgid "Pilot control of the gimbal can be restored by setting up an :ref:`auxiliary function switch <common-auxiliary-functions>` either “Retract Mount1” (i.e. RCx_OPTION = 27) or \"Retract Mount2\" (i.e. RCx_OPTION = 113), and then move the switch to the lower position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:125
#: 2f81bdabf13d41f8a35666931f923236
msgid "Updating the gimbal software"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:127
#: 35b2a84fcf404b0eb00c6a148c9cf3e9
msgid "The gimbal must be running firmware version 1.4 or higher. Follow the instructions below to update both the controller and motor firmwares."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:129
#: b222126b469045379e54be2eb9667101
msgid "Connect the gimbal to your computer using the USB dongle. Ensure that the gimbal end is plugged into the \"Gimbal Controller Connector\" (see diagram in the Connecting the Gimbal to the Pixhawk section above). Leave the gimbal unpowered for now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:130
#: 81bb1ca8a5684340bc8910804b19bffe
msgid "Start the \"ZYX-BMGC-EN_V1.5\" configuration application"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:131
#: 18991f83951c45c5847e79f0d7903761
msgid "Select **Open Firmware** and select the **../Firmware_V1.5/Gimbal Controller Firmware V1.5.bgsf** file from the `Tarot Gimbal Firmware v1.5 zip. <https://download.ardupilot.org/downloads/wiki/advanced_user_tools/ZYX-BMGC-EN_V1.5.zip>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:132
#: 0e333883dc0a4ce1be906e7716791946
msgid "Select the COM Port that has been assigned to the gimbal, then select \"Open COM Port.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:133
#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:140
#: 411768bc7f0d4738b3e43265a211684a
#: 9faa5314eae84a4a80f50efd9459d18c
msgid "Select **Start Upgrade**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:134
#: e9d9cc53ead54a35b87e1235da3d4fe3
msgid "Connect the battery to power the gimbal. You will see a green progress bar on the screen indicating the status of the update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:135
#: 8dbce03852d5481897fed7941212bdca
msgid "To verify that the firmware has updated successfully, disconnect and reconnect the battery. Select **Open COM Port**, and check that the version firmware number now displays the updated version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:136
#: 3cf06be0348647b999bc6cd039e9c88b
msgid "Now you'll need to update the motor firmware. Disconnect the battery from the gimbal so that it is not powered. Disconnect the USB dongle from the \"Gimbal Controller Connector\" and reconnect to the \"Motor Driver Connector\" on the other side of the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:137
#: 1ccd0efea8584a0cb8980b1e3d32788c
msgid "Select **Motor Configuration**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:138
#: 393cc24552bd4e27875b08ea7f472a0f
msgid "Select **Open COM Port**. Ensure that the same COM port as before is selected (the gimbal controller and motor controller use the same COM port)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:139
#: cf5672cbb0484163b973f8ac0202e692
msgid "Now select **Open Firmware**, but this time select the **../Firmware_V1.5/Motor Driver Firmware V1.5.bmcf** file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:141
#: 1286903ddd624bcd85e4528f08d052c8
msgid "Connect the battery to power the gimbal. There will be another progress bar indicating the status of the upgrade."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:142
#: 0365f6e68d30406a8d2c66110c9b1284
msgid "Disconnect and reconnect the battery from the gimbal to complete the upgrade process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tarot-gimbal.rst:143
#: fbdc4e2b63e840d998769547d1006bcf
msgid "You may need to check/set the configuration settings again, as above. In particular, check that the manual control mode is \"Stick Position Mode\" and remember to write your settings when you're done!"
msgstr ""
